1
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Shine brighter. Shine farther.

2
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Life-Size 2 is a family, fantasy film directed by Steven K. Tsuchida.

3
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Grace Manning is in the middle of her quarter-life crisis,
realizing she is in over her head as CEO.

4
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
To make matters worse, her wild-child ways are
causing the company’s stock to plummet.

5
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
With the help of her young next-door neighbor, Grace’s old Eve doll magically awakens to help get Grace
back on track and give her the confidence to be the woman and leader Eve knows Grace can be.

6
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Eve, played by Tyra Banks.

7
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Grace Martin, played by Francia Raísa.

8
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Calum, played by Gavin Stenhouse.

9
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Brendan Butler, played by Hank Chen.

10
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Lex, played by Alison Fernández.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Tahlia, played by Shanica Knowles.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Life-Size 2, also known as Life-Size 2: A Christmas Eve, is a 2018 American fantasy-comedy
television film directed by Steven Tsuchida and starring Tyra Banks and Francia Raisa.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
It is the sequel to Life-Size starring Banks and Lindsay Lohan, which originally
premiered in 2000 on ABC as part of The Wonderful World of Disney.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The sequel was produced by Banks, Stephanie Allain, Roger M.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
Bobb, and Angi Bones.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It premiered during Freeform's 25 Days of Christmas, on December 2, 2018.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
In February 2020, Banks revealed she was working on Life-Size 3.
